    "summary": "Model completed and passing all L1/L2/L3 checks.\n\nStructure: single simply-supported span, 30 m bearing-centre-to-centre, spine-beam 2D idealization, three precast prestressed small-box girders per span (C40). Section integrated to A_single = 1.13893 m², I_single = 0.35492 m⁴; per MR-02 the assembled girder properties are A = 3.41679 m² and I = 1.06475 m⁴ (3 girders). Unit weight 26 kN/m³, Ec = 32500 MPa; self weight w = 88.836 kN/m, m = 9.0557 t/m (girder self-weight only).\n\nSupports: two abutments, each on 6 plain laminated elastomeric bearings (2 per girder end × 3 girders; 300×400 mm, 5 × 8 mm rubber layers). Shape factor S = 10.71; Kv = 8.518e6 kN/m, Kh = 18000 kN/m, rotation free at each line.\n\nLive load: Highway Class II, two design lanes, qk = 7.875 kN/m, Pk = 240 kN, ξ = 1.0.\n\nKey results: fundamental vertical frequency f1 = 3.402 Hz → impact factor μ = 0.2006 (JTG D60-2015 4.3.2); self-weight support reactions 1332.5 kN each (sum 2665 kN = γ·A·L); self-weight mid-span moment 9994 kN·m; lane-load max positive moment 6449.6 kN·m.\n\nRoot cause of the initial failure: the accepted girder.A decision held the single-girder area (1.1389 m²) instead of the assembled 3-girder area, contradicting MR-02 and the already-consistent girder.I, girder.w and girder.m; this tripped the L2-1 traceability/recompute check. Revising girder.A to 3.41679 m² (per MR-02, A = A_single × n_girders) and regenerating the model made all checks pass."
